      the more specific peeled/cut material proposal. Starting potato masses are process
      input amounts, not measured retained solids in a filtrate. FOODON 03315354 names
      a potato tuber; FOODON 00002796 covers whole/piece derivatives, but no exact
      claim erases a recipe-specific preparation.
notes: '#1201 isolated proposal: Potato material supplied as tuber tissue in the linked
  recipes. The material input is distinct from liquid potato infusion or extract after
  boiling and filtration. Case 16 occurrences carrying peeled-and-cut notes are additionally
  bound to the more specific peeled/cut material proposal. Starting potato masses
  are process input amounts, not measured retained solids in a filtrate. FOODON 03315354
  names a potato tuber; FOODON 00002796 covers whole/piece derivatives, but no exact
  claim erases a recipe-specific preparation. Extraction yield and tissue removal
  vary by recipe; no single output preparation or finished-medium potato concentration
  is asserted. Raw source spellings are retained in case evidence and this source
  scope; no new globally resolving source-local alias is added. Full-owner publication
  approval and all source-specific holds remain pending.'
